From: Holodor <holodor@bonesaw.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Dynamic refresh for panels without an EDID

DSI panels (Retroid Pocket 5: 1080x1920 at 60 and 120 Hz) have no EDID
property, so ParseEDID() returned before the code that offers the panel's
other refresh rates to Steam. gamescope then reported one valid rate and
Steam had no refresh control.

Offer every refresh rate the connector lists at its preferred resolution
when there is no EDID, the same as for an unknown display that has one.

GAMESCOPE_DYNAMIC_REFRESH_PREFER_LOWEST=1 makes an app fps target pick the
lowest matching panel rate instead of the highest. On a 60/120 Hz panel a
60 fps target then runs the panel at 60 Hz, one frame per refresh, instead
of every second refresh at 120 Hz.

GAMESCOPE_DYNAMIC_REFRESH_DEFAULT_LOWEST=1 (convar dynamic_refresh_default_lowest,
changeable with gamescopectl) runs the panel at its lowest rate
when no app target is set (Steam UI, uncapped games); a target that divides
a higher rate still switches up.
